34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our ""ambitious"" projects often slip by a year, while the necessary repairs stay on track. We must be careful.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found something worrying! We have specialist rooms sitting empty, but general rooms are totally full. We are building the wrong things!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,My findings are concerning. Our technicians are wasting hours on manual routines that should be automated. The workload is unsustainable.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've discovered that projects designed for a single department often fail to satisfy users. We need flexible, shared spaces to ensure success.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How fascinating. It appears our tender records show costs rising significantly, yet our budget requests remain stubbornly static. We are dreaming in a vacuum.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that explains why the schedules get squeezed. When the money runs out, the time is sacrificed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"And @Mizuki, that matches what I saw! If we build a specialist room that no one uses, it's just a waste of space.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"If we choose a plan that requires more manual upkeep, we are simply punishing the few staff members we have left.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"I also noticed that the older blocks are a gamble. If we touch those walls, we risk hitting hazardous materials and delaying everything.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. Furthermore, we have equipment that has completely depreciated with no reserve for replacement. We are essentially operating on a deficit of reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I noticed that weather delays are a huge factor for external work. Perhaps an internal renovation is safer for our timeline?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"But we have to think about the students! If we close rooms for internal work, the timetable records show we end up paying for off-site space.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I am not interested in the aesthetics. I want a plan that includes automated systems to replace these manual routines.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We must balance that. A high-tech system is useless if the post-occupancy reviews show that the staff find it too complex to use.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests we avoid any plan with a high ""market volatility"" risk. If the tender for a project is likely to spike, we should avoid it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I just want us to be honest with the university about how long things take. Let's choose the most predictable option.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I just want everyone to have a place to study! Let's pick the plan that increases general-purpose capacity without killing the timetable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I will support any plan that reduces the physical burden on the bench technicians. That is my priority.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I will support a plan that is flexible and serves a wide range of users, provided it doesn't risk a hazardous material disaster.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall vote for the plan that is most fiscally transparent and least likely to result in a budget overrun that we'll only discover after the ribbon is cut.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
