60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Plan A is entirely outdoors. Given the weather delays I found, that seems very risky for our schedule.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Plan C is perfect! It creates general study space, which is exactly what the booking data says we are missing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Plan D is the only one that addresses the technicians' burden. New ventilation and layouts would eliminate those manual routines.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Plan C is in an older block. My survey findings suggest we might hit hazardous materials, which would be a disaster for the timeline.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan B involves high-end AV equipment. Given that we have no renewal reserves for such kit, it is a financial time bomb.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, is Plan D internal? If it is, it avoids the weather risks of Plan A. But is it a ""comfort"" project or a ""necessity""?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, I understand the risk, but the students are struggling now! We can't just ignore the demand for study space.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"It is a necessity, Shizue. The staff are exhausted. If we don't automate the extraction and layout, we will lose our technicians.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, I care about the students, but a project that stalls for six months due to asbestos is worse than no project at all.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Plan D's mechanical plant is where the tender spikes are most severe. It is the most likely to exceed the budget by twenty percent.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,Plan C is a conversion of an existing hall. That usually has a more predictable delivery schedule than a full mechanical overhaul.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly! And it doesn't require the expensive, specialized equipment that Benjamin is worried about in Plan B.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I cannot in good conscience support a plan that ignores the people doing the actual work. Plan D is the only responsible choice for the staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Plan B is a shared resource. My post-occupancy data shows that shared, bookable spaces are the most successful. It's a safer bet for user satisfaction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan C is the most modest in terms of market risk. It is mostly furniture and partitions, not volatile mechanical plant or high-end electronics.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I feel Plan C is the most balanced. It is internal, avoiding weather, and less complex than Plan D, making the schedule more reliable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we're leaning toward Plan C! It's exactly what the students need and it's a positive change for the campus.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I will remain stubborn on this. The technicians cannot wait another year. I will vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I am torn, but the risk of hazardous materials in Plan C is too high. I will vote for Plan B; it's a shared space and avoids the old block's walls.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While Plan B is a shared space, the lack of renewal reserves makes it a liability. Plan C is the only logical choice for budget stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
